.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/jiti Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "jiti"
.PP
\fR\fP \fR\fP \fR\fP \fR\fP

.PP
Runtime Typescript and ESM support for Node\&.js\&.

.PP
\fBImportant\fP
.RS 4
This is the support branch for jiti v1\&. Check out \fRjiti/main\fP for the latest version and \fRunjs/jiti#174\fP for the roadmap\&.
.RE
.PP
.SH "Features"
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Seamless typescript and ESM syntax support
.IP "\(bu" 2
Seamless interoperability between ESM and CommonJS
.IP "\(bu" 2
Synchronous API to replace \fRrequire\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Super slim and zero dependency
.IP "\(bu" 2
Smart syntax detection to avoid extra transforms
.IP "\(bu" 2
CommonJS cache integration
.IP "\(bu" 2
Filesystem transpile hard cache
.IP "\(bu" 2
V8 compile cache
.IP "\(bu" 2
Custom resolve alias
.PP
.SH "Usage"
.PP
.SS "Programmatic"
.PP
.nf
const jiti = require("jiti")(__filename);

jiti("\&./path/to/file\&.ts");
.fi
.PP

.PP
You can also pass options as second argument:

.PP
.PP
.nf
const jiti = require("jiti")(__filename, { debug: true });
.fi
.PP
.SS "CLI"
.PP
.nf
jiti index\&.ts
# or npx jiti index\&.ts
.fi
.PP
.SS "Register require hook"
.PP
.nf
node \-r jiti/register index\&.ts
.fi
.PP

.PP
Alternatively, you can register \fRjiti\fP as a require hook programmatically:

.PP
.PP
.nf
const jiti = require("jiti")();
const unregister = jiti\&.register();
.fi
.PP
.SH "Options"
.PP
.SS "\fRdebug\fP"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: Boolean
.IP "\(bu" 2
Default: \fRfalse\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Environment Variable: \fRJITI_DEBUG\fP
.PP

.PP
Enable debug to see which files are transpiled
.SS "\fRcache\fP"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: Boolean | String
.IP "\(bu" 2
Default: \fRtrue\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Environment Variable: \fRJITI_CACHE\fP
.PP

.PP
Use transpile cache

.PP
If set to \fRtrue\fP will use \fRnode_modules/\&.cache/jiti\fP (if exists) or \fR{TMP_DIR}/node-jiti\fP
.SS "\fResmResolve\fP"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: Boolean | String
.IP "\(bu" 2
Default: \fRfalse\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Environment Variable: \fRJITI_ESM_RESOLVE\fP
.PP

.PP
Using esm resolution algorithm to support \fRimport\fP condition\&.
.SS "\fRtransform\fP"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: Function
.IP "\(bu" 2
Default: Babel (lazy loaded)
.PP

.PP
Transform function\&. See \fRsrc/babel\fP for more details
.SS "\fRsourceMaps\fP"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: Boolean
.IP "\(bu" 2
Default \fRfalse\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Environment Variable: \fRJITI_SOURCE_MAPS\fP
.PP

.PP
Add inline source map to transformed source for better debugging\&.
.SS "\fRinteropDefault\fP"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: Boolean
.IP "\(bu" 2
Default: \fRfalse\fP
.PP

.PP
Return the \fR\&.default\fP export of a module at the top-level\&.
.SS "\fRalias\fP"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: Object
.IP "\(bu" 2
Default: -
.IP "\(bu" 2
Environment Variable: \fRJITI_ALIAS\fP
.PP

.PP
Custom alias map used to resolve ids\&.
.SS "\fRnativeModules\fP"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: Array
.IP "\(bu" 2
Default: ['typescript\fR]\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fREnvironment Variable: \fPJITI_NATIVE_MODULES`
.PP

.PP
List of modules (within \fRnode_modules\fP) to always use native require for them\&.
.SS "\fRtransformModules\fP"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: Array
.IP "\(bu" 2
Default: []
.IP "\(bu" 2
Environment Variable: \fRJITI_TRANSFORM_MODULES\fP
.PP

.PP
List of modules (within \fRnode_modules\fP) to transform them regardless of syntax\&.
.SS "\fRexperimentalBun\fP"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Type: Boolean
.IP "\(bu" 2
Default: Enabled if \fRprocess\&.versions\&.bun\fP exists (Bun runtime)
.IP "\(bu" 2
Environment Variable: \fRJITI_EXPERIMENTAL_BUN\fP
.PP

.PP
Enable experimental native Bun support for transformations\&.
.SH "Development"
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Clone this repository
.IP "\(bu" 2
Enable \fRCorepack\fP using \fRcorepack enable\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Install dependencies using \fRpnpm install\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Run \fRpnpm dev\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Run \fRpnpm jiti \&./test/path/to/file\&.ts\fP
.PP
